{"author":{"id":"0f3f15615bd1cd3a554838fa7b24a3097d93824fce4381669b4f2c617b4d3f60"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1761929062,"nonce":"OCgkc/alv5iVTktcIgA30oA0f70=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOCGKeh87VIH1Y","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/1490","origin":"github"},"title":"Feature request: add \"list\" command (synonym to / instead of \"bug\")","message":"Currently there is just a \"git-bug bug\" command to list all known issues.\n\nBut as an issue is not always a bug, but could also be a change or feature request, IMHO \"bug\" as a command to list all issues is somehow misplaced. It should be \"list\", which is more logical, like:\n\n~~~shell\ngit-bug list\n~~~\n\nCould you set \"list\" as a synonym for \"bug\", or even consider replacing \"bug\" with \"list\"?","files":null}]}